Profile (JSON file - profiles.json):
  name: str
  mode: "sniper" | "ar_smg" | "shotgun"
  trigger: "lclick" | "xbutton1" | "xbutton2"
  sniper_delays: list[int] (4 values, 0-200ms)
  shotgun_delays: list[int] (2 values, 0-200ms)
  ar_smg_delay: int (0-200ms)
  switch_method: "qq" | "31"
  key_hold_delay: int (0-200ms)
  recoil: bool
  recoil_amount: int (1-20)
  recoil_smooth: bool
  recoil_timeout_ms: int (500-3000)

Engine State (engine/_state.py):
  _listening, _running, _trigger_held: bool
  _stop_macro: threading.Event
  _cfg: dict (runtime copy of config.DEFAULT)
  _hook, _hook_proc, _hook_thread, _hook_thread_id  (Windows only)
  _macro_thread: Thread
  _pb_hwnd, _trigger_blocked
  _log_callback, _status_callback, _action_callback: callable
  _shortcut_running: bool
  _shortcut_prev: dict (key → bool debounce)

Platform Backends (engine/_plat_*.py):
  _plat_win32.py:
    Input: SendInput via ctypes (user32.dll)
    Hook: WH_MOUSE_LL (SetWindowsHookEx)
    Shortcuts: GetAsyncKeyState polling
  _plat_linux.py:
    Input: ydotool subprocess
    Hook: evdev /dev/input polling (needs input group)
    Shortcuts: evdev /dev/input key state polling

Layer Dependency:
  app/ → engine/* → engine/_plat_* (via sys.platform dispatch)
  macros.py is platform-agnostic, uses click_left/right/press_key from input_sim
